  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Each player is dealt one card face down. Without looking, players hold the card to their forehead so all other players can see it. A round of poker betting follows (fold, check, bet, call, raise). After betting, remaining players showdown. The highest card wins the pot; ties split the pot. There is no suit order for breaking ties.',
    Player: 'Each player is dealt one card face down. Without looking, players hold the card to their forehead so all other players can see it. A round of poker betting follows (fold, check, bet, call, raise). After betting, remaining players showdown. The highest card wins the pot; ties split the pot. There is no suit order for breaking ties.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest card among players who did not fold at showdown; if tied, split the pot.',
    gameplay: 'Each player is dealt one card face down. Without looking, players hold the card to their forehead so all other players can see it. A round of poker betting follows (fold, check, bet, call, raise). After betting, remaining players showdown. The highest card wins the pot; ties split the pot. There is no suit order for breaking ties.',
    keyRules: [
      'One card each, held to forehead facing outward so others see it; players do not look at their own card.',
      'Players ante, then a round of poker betting.',
      'Highest card at showdown wins the pot; ties split the pot; no suit order.',
    ],
